  "course_description": "An introduction to the reading and interpretation of a variety of literary and cultural media including poetry, drama, prose fiction, political writings, publicity, films, painting, and architecture.",
  "course_notes": "FREN 314 Reading Across Media. Professor Valérie Loichot (TTh 1:00-2:15pm). Content: This class proposes an introduction to French literary studies with a focus on close reading and textual analysis. Its objective is to provide students with methodological foundations and tools that will allow them to engage creatively with texts from different periods and in different genres. Those genres may include fairytales, verse and prose poetry, classical tragedy, a nineteenth-century short story, essayistic literature, paintings, music, and films.",
